             weakly clipped by a circular aperture, which stays close to a
             Gaussian with changed parameters. With the waist in the
             aperture plane and a relative power loss u = dP/P, the
             equivalent waist shrinks by 1 - sqrt(u), the divergence grows
             by 1/(1 - sqrt(u)) and the fictitious waist intensity by
